## Whole-day delay per test day (mean over replications) and twin capacity check

Capacity check: GDOT's PM plan C gives Piedmont-from-N through (P8, 2 lanes) 48.4 s of green per 180 s. At the twin's discharge rate (about 1920 veh/h per lane of green; intersections/7065/timing/capacity_check/README.md) that is about 1033 veh/h. 'v/c' = that day's counted PM peak hour / this capacity; above 1 the queue under real timing grows through the PM. The last column is the resulting PM delay of that movement under real timing (actuated). GDOT's detectors counted these vehicles passing, so where the twin can't carry them the real-timing number reflects the twin and the counts (some PM bins look inflated by set-back count detectors), not GDOT's controller.

